[{:adr/authoritative_for ["landing-record ADR for ADR-2607102300's Phase 1 (GTG field equations),\n    mirroring the ADR-2607101700 -> ADR-2607101900 scope-then-landing pattern" "landed 2026-07-09: kotoba-lang/standard-model#9 merged as\n    3710b427ed90b0a7afce3a08b00212bda8b7bcd8, 68 tests/2740 assertions\n    (up from 58/2465 at ADR-2607101900's close), CI green JDK 17+21;\n    superproject pin advanced via API single-entry commit\n    d8bb964afa3555a7ba691790ebdd08049d56d7a1" "three-pass history: (1) literature research cross-verified LDG 1998 primary\n    (gr-qc/0405033) + independent author Francis-Kosowsky (gr-qc/0311007) on the\n    vacuum action, Omega-field equation (eq 4.37/4.40), closed-form solution\n    (eq 4.49-4.53), and LDG's own Schwarzschild worked example (eq 6.79/6.73);\n    (2) a first standalone numeric verification FAILED and correctly diagnosed\n    why -- pdftotext extraction of eq 4.28/4.49-4.53 was garbled, AND the wrong\n    covariant derivative was used (Phase 0a's flat rotation-gauge-only D_mu\n    instead of the calligraphic D from Table 2 using hbar(grad) and\n    omega(a)=Omega(h(a))) -- reusing the wrong operator builds a teleparallel\n    connection with IDENTICALLY ZERO curvature by construction, a structurally\n    wrong equation not a sign slip; (3) reading actual PDF PAGE IMAGES (not text\n    extraction) resolved this, and a standalone Python/numpy verification\n    reproduced LDG's closed-form Schwarzschild curvature (eq 6.73) to ~1e-13,\n    Ricci=0 to 1e-17 to 1e-19 at 3 points -- clearing ADR-2607102300's\n    verification bar, independently re-run and confirmed by the requester before\n    Clojure implementation began" "Clojure port (PR #9) landed: frame-adjoint (eq 2.46, self-inverse h<->hbar\n    adjoint), minimal new GA primitives on existing kotoba.sm.tensor\n    (bivector<->matrix, wedge-vectors, vector-dot-bivector, bivector-commutator,\n    outermorphism -- no from-scratch GA engine), H-field+omega-from-h (eq\n    4.49/4.53, vacuum spin-free closed-form Omega(h)), L-a-omega+riemann-basis-pair\n    +riemann-map-matrix+riemann-map (eq 4.48, the COVARIANT Riemann map using\n    position-gauge-covariant L_a, not Phase 0a's flat derivative), curvature-scalar\n    (true LDG Ricci scalar R=sum_ab gamma^a.(gamma^b.R(h_b^h_a)), using the FIXED\n    background frame's own trivial reciprocal per Phase 0d's 2-source literature\n    finding -- reachable only because riemann-map supplies the previously-missing\n    bilinear extension to general bivectors)" "before merge, requester independently re-derived Schwarzschild regression\n    numbers in a live Clojure REPL session -- caught and corrected a mistake in\n    that independent re-derivation itself (forgot the hbar->h frame-adjoint\n    conversion on first attempt, giving spuriously near-zero results), landing\n    on values matching committed tests to the same tolerance after correction" "verification landed WITH the code: Schwarzschild regression at 2 independent\n    points/masses (error ~1e-9 to 1e-10, within FD tolerance), curvature-scalar\n    approx 0 at both (expected vacuum result) and EXACTLY 0.0 at flat limit\n    (h=position-gauge-identity, every derivative vanishes identically)" "QUALITATIVE SCOPE CHANGE from every prior ADR: ADR-2607051500 through\n    ADR-2607101900 all framed this repo as classical field algebra only, NOT an\n    action/field-equation engine -- that framing no longer fully applies, this\n    repo now contains a genuine field EQUATION (vacuum Omega(h)) and its\n    physical consequence (curvature scalar verified against an exact solution).\n    What has NOT changed: still bounded to vacuum/spin-free, verified against\n    exactly ONE exact solution (Schwarzschild) not a general GR-equivalence\n    proof, and every ADR-2607102300 boundary (matter coupling, Einstein\n    multivector/stress-energy sourcing i.e. non-vacuum G(a)=kappa*T(a),\n    spin/torsion via full eq 4.28, quantization/RGE/scattering/lattice,\n    dark-sector/de-Sitter) remains out of scope, not implicitly widened" "methodological note: this is the SECOND time in this repo's history (after\n    PR #6's self-interaction-term slot-order bug) that a seemingly-thorough\n    single pass produced a confidently-wrong result that failed SILENTLY\n    (identically-zero curvature, no error thrown) rather than loudly -- caught\n    only because the success criterion was an independent numeric match against\n    a known closed-form result, not merely 'does the code run' or 'does the\n    formula resemble the paper'. Not license to relax this discipline for\n    future phases."], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kotoba-lang-standard-model", :adr/related ["adr-2607102300" "adr-2607101900" "adr-2607101700" "adr-2607051500"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607102700-kotoba-lang-standard-model-gtg-phase1-landing", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-09", :adr/body "see 2607102700-kotoba-lang-standard-model-gtg-phase1-landing.md", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-09", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607102700: kotoba-lang/standard-model — Phase 1 landing: the vacuum Omega(h) field equation, covariant Riemann map, and the true LDG Ricci scalar"}]